  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:5445",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N appears to be a target for multiple pathways that ultimately lead to S-117. The evidence suggests that Mollicellin N interacts with 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which is a known target of several molecules, including the common target of A704 and Ubiquitin carboxyl-terminal hydrolase 5. These findings indicate that Mollicellin N may act as a modulator or inhibitor of a metabolic pathway that ultimately affects S-117. The consistent presence of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid as a common intermediate in these relationships suggests a potential biochemical mechanism involving lipid metabolism. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid as a central mediator in the interaction between Mollicellin N and S-117, potentially through a shared metabolic or signaling pathway.",
